                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Bought it to try out the AR implementation.\n\nGood try, but much like you'd expect, the Vive camera isn't useful for AR stuff in general. The biggest problem is it's monoscopic. With no depth from the camera, your real hand will render behind the camera and seem gigantic by comparison, throwing off any sense of scale to the environment.\n\nThe real effect of AR in VR right now is that it's some VR stuff rendered on top of a low resolution, grainy, monoscopic 360 video sphere that you kinda recognize as a rough low res facsimile  of the world just outside of the headset; rather than feeling like virtual objects are been rendered on top of the real world, as is the true goal of AR.\n\n2 dollars is the right price for this. Very rough around the edges, but a decent answer to how AR feels in VR right now.",
